Byte-by-byte Description of file: table.dat
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Bytes Format Units  Label     Explanations
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1- 19  A19    ---    star     Star designation as in source table
 21- 43  A23    ---    sample   Source sample identifier
     45  A1     ---    tier     A: spectroscopic logg; B: MIST-track mass
                               placement
 47- 51  F5.3   [K]    logTeff  [3.53/4.77] log10 effective temperature
 53- 57  F5.3   [-]    logLspec [2.33/4.59] log10 spectroscopic luminosity
                               Teff^4/g, solar units (5777^4/274/100)
 59- 67  E9.4   ---    alpha0   [0.0/16275.18]? Red-noise amplitude at zero
                               frequency (unit per sample, see Table 1)
     69  I1     ---    a0flag   1 if alpha0 is umag-compatible and used in
                               amplitude analysis
 71- 77  F7.5   d-1    nuchar   [0.06/9.06] Characteristic frequency
 79- 83  F5.3   ---    gamma    [0.81/5.1]? High-frequency logarithmic slope
 85- 88  F4.1   km.s-1 vsini    [7.0/370.0]? Projected rotational velocity
 90- 97  F8.6   ---    tau      [0.0/1.17] Fractional main-sequence age from
                               MIST (>1 = post-MS)
 99-107  F9.6   [Msun] logM     [-0.03/2.15] log10 current mass from MIST
109-114  F6.4   [Rsun] logR     [0.28/2.98] log10 radius from MIST
116-123  F8.6   d-1    frot     [0.0/0.93]? vsini/(2 pi R), lower limit on
                               rotation frequency
    125  I1     ---    rotflag  1 if nuchar within 0.15 dex of frot or 2 frot
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
